extend type Query {
  """Paginated snapshot of supported logistics entities of one force in a bounded area: transport belts, underground belts, splitters, loaders, linked belts, inserters, pipes, pipe-to-ground, storage tanks, boilers, pumps and offshore pumps. surface and force must be non-empty and exist; area sides must be positive and at most 1024 tiles. type, when non-empty, must be one of those entity types and narrows the page to that type, while pageInfo.total stays the matching count before pagination (limit 1 through 10000, default 100, offset zero-based). Belt-like entities carry lanes with engine transport-line names, sides and contents; inserters carry pickup/drop positions and the held stack; every entity carries engine status, fluid boxes and fuel/output inventories where they exist. Entries are sorted by type, prototype name, position and unit number, and pageInfo.hasMore reports further pages; all entities in a page are read at one tick."""
  worldLogistics(input: WorldLogisticsInput!): WorldLogisticsPage!
  """Belt-family tile census of one surface inside a bounded area: every matching transport belt, underground belt, splitter, loader, loader-1x1, and linked belt of every force, with per-lane contents and mixed flags. surface must exist; area sides must be positive and at most 1024 tiles. types is optional: null or empty selects every belt-family type, otherwise every listed name must be one of the six belt-family types and an unknown name is rejected before any engine read. Entries are sorted by position y, then x, then unit number. limit is 1 through 10000 (default 1000) and offset is zero-based; pageInfo.total and total are the true matching count before pagination, so one call with limit 10000 returns the whole census."""
  beltTiles(input: BeltTilesInput!): BeltTilesPage!
  """Paginated snapshot of resource entities, obstacles and pumpable water tiles in a bounded area of one force, with nearby selected-force mining drills. surface and force must be non-empty and exist; area sides must be positive and at most 1024 tiles. resourceName filters resource entities only (never obstacles or water); kinds, when non-empty, keeps only the listed entry kinds (resource, tree, cliff, simple-entity, water) and narrows pageInfo.total, while resourceTotal, obstacleTotal and waterTotal remain whole-area counts independent of the kinds filter. Water counts only tiles that collide with water_tile and expose a pumpable fluid, so out-of-map tiles are excluded. drillRadius (0 to 1000 tiles, default 10) finds drills by distance from each resource entry; groupPatches instead clusters matching resource entities into adjacency-connected patches sorted by finite amount descending, and a patch's nearbyDrills only include drills whose mining area (mining_drill_radius around the drill, falling back to drillRadius) actually covers at least one tile of that patch, so a drill beside a patch it cannot mine is not reported and each listed drill carries its engine status and covered tile/amount counts. Patches are returned in full and not paginated. Infinite resources such as crude oil carry a yield percentage instead of a finite amount, so their patch reports infinite true, yieldPercent summed over its tiles, and totalAmount 0; clippedByArea marks a patch that touches the scan boundary, which means its tiles and amounts are partial. Entry-level nearby drills are distance matches, not proof of mining coverage; limit (1 through 10000, default 100) and zero-based offset paginate the sorted entries."""
  worldResources(input: WorldResourcesInput!): WorldResourcesPage!
  """Ask the engine's surface.can_place_entity whether one entity prototype of the selected force fits at a position and direction. surface, force and prototype must be non-empty and exist; position must be finite and direction is an engine direction code from 0 to 15. The check is the engine's manual build check, the same rules a player placing by hand gets (collisions plus prototype rules such as offshore pumps needing water), so player reach, inventory and researched technology are still not considered. When the placement is refused, blockers lists the colliding prototype names found anywhere in the prototype's footprint (deduplicated and sorted), and terrain is true when any footprint tile's own collision mask shares a layer with the prototype; both are empty and false when canPlace is true. tile is the ground tile name under the position in either case."""
  worldPlacement(input: WorldPlacementInput!): WorldPlacementResult!
  """Sample engine placement legality for one entity prototype on every tile center of a bounded area and return it in the shape selected by mode: blocked tiles with their blockers, a compact placeability grid, or the largest empty rectangles. surface, force and prototype must be non-empty and exist; direction is a direction code from 0 to 15; area sides must be positive and at most 1024 tiles, and the sampled tile count (columns times rows) may not exceed 262144. Checks use the engine's manual build check, the same rules a player placing by hand gets, so offshore pumps need water and pumpjacks need an oil field; a tile holding a real entity is refused whatever the direction, matching the plain placement occupancy rule, so a belt on a belt reads as blocked even where the engine would fast-replace it. The occupancy rule is the plain placement one: a tile is blocked only by an entity whose collision mask intersects the prototype's mask, so resources, ghosts, item stacks and corpses (including the tree stumps Factorio 2.0 leaves behind after mining a tree, whose mask is the tiles-only doodad layer) do not block and belts stay placeable over ore or a stump. All engine checks run in every mode: blockedTiles is filled only in BLOCKED_TILES (the default) and is empty otherwise, with each refused tile listing the blockers found anywhere in the prototype's footprint and terrain true when any footprint tile blocks it; rows only in GRID (one string per tile row, top row first, one character per tile, 1 placeable and 0 blocked), and sites only in SITES (greedy largest-first, non-overlapping rectangles of at least siteWidth by siteHeight tiles with the origin at the top-left tile corner; siteWidth/siteHeight must not exceed the area and maxSites is 1 through 1000). sampled, placeable and blocked are always filled. Player reach, inventory and research are not considered."""
  probePlacement(input: PlacementProbeInput!): PlacementProbeResult!
}

"""Area coordinates must be finite; positive dimensions must each be at most 1024 tiles. Limit is 1 through 10000; offset is zero-based and non-negative. Type is optional: null or empty selects every supported logistics entity type, otherwise it must be one of transport-belt, underground-belt, splitter, loader, loader-1x1, linked-belt, inserter, pipe, pipe-to-ground, storage-tank, boiler, pump or offshore-pump. surface defaults to nauvis, force defaults to player, and limit defaults to 100."""
input WorldLogisticsInput { surface: String! = "nauvis" force: String! = "player" area: FactoryAreaInput! type: String limit: Int! = 100 offset: Int! = 0 }
"""Belt-family tile census of one surface inside a bounded area. surface defaults to nauvis and must exist; area sides must be positive and at most 1024 tiles. types is optional: null or empty selects every belt-family type (transport-belt, underground-belt, splitter, loader, loader-1x1, linked-belt), otherwise every listed name must be one of them, and an unknown name is rejected before any engine read. Entries are every matching belt-family entity of every force, sorted by position y, then x, then unit number. limit is 1 through 10000 (default 1000) and offset is zero-based; pageInfo.total and total are the true matching count before pagination, so one call with limit 10000 returns the whole census."""
input BeltTilesInput { surface: String! = "nauvis" area: FactoryAreaInput! types: [String!] limit: Int! = 1000 offset: Int! = 0 }
"""Area has the same bounds and pagination constraints as WorldLogisticsInput. Drill radius is finite and between 0 and 1000 tiles. Resource name filters resources only, not obstacles or water. Kinds, when non-empty, keeps only the listed entry kinds (resource, tree, cliff, simple-entity, water) and narrows total; the resource, obstacle and water partition totals stay unfiltered counts for the whole area. GroupPatches clusters matching resource entities into connected patches regardless of the kinds filter."""
input WorldResourcesInput { surface: String! = "nauvis" force: String! = "player" area: FactoryAreaInput! resourceName: String drillRadius: Float! = 10 kinds: [String!] groupPatches: Boolean! = false limit: Int! = 100 offset: Int! = 0 }
"""Surface, force and prototype must be non-empty and exist; coordinates must be finite and direction must be between 0 and 15."""
input WorldPlacementInput { surface: String! = "nauvis" force: String! = "player" prototype: String! position: PositionInput! direction: Int! = 0 }
"""Selects which result list a placement probe fills. BLOCKED_TILES reports every refused tile with its blockers. GRID reports a compact row-major placeability map. SITES reports the largest non-overlapping empty tile rectangles that are at least siteWidth by siteHeight, largest first."""
enum PlacementProbeMode { BLOCKED_TILES GRID SITES }
"""Surface, force and prototype must be non-empty and exist; direction must be between 0 and 15. Area bounds match WorldResourcesInput, but the sampled tile count may not exceed 262144. mode selects which result list is filled (BLOCKED_TILES -> blockedTiles, GRID -> rows, SITES -> sites); siteWidth/siteHeight/maxSites only affect SITES and are tile counts from 1 to the area dimensions, maxSites 1 through 1000."""
input PlacementProbeInput { surface: String! = "nauvis" force: String! = "player" prototype: String! direction: Int! = 0 area: FactoryAreaInput! mode: PlacementProbeMode! = BLOCKED_TILES siteWidth: Float! = 1 siteHeight: Float! = 1 maxSites: Int! = 50 }

type WorldArea { leftTopX: Float! leftTopY: Float! rightBottomX: Float! rightBottomY: Float! }
"""One transport line of a belt-like entity. lineName is the engine defines.transport_line name (for example left_line, right_line, secondary_left_line on an underground belt, or a splitter line) and side is left, right, or unknown when the name is unrecognised. Indexes are 1-based and per entity type: 2 for a transport belt, 4 for an underground belt (surface plus tunnel lines), 8 for a splitter. mixed is true when this lane holds more than one distinct item prototype or quality combination, which is lane contamination rather than a full lane; it is always false for an empty lane."""
type WorldLane { index: Int! lineName: String! side: String! items: [InventoryStack!]! mixed: Boolean! }
"""One-based fluid box index and capacity; name, amount and temperature are null for an empty box."""
type WorldFluid { index: Int! name: String amount: Float temperature: Float capacity: Float! }
type WorldInventory { kind: String! items: [InventoryStack!]! }
"""One logistics entity. undergroundType and pairedUnitNumber are filled only for underground-belt halves: undergroundType is INPUT or OUTPUT and pairedUnitNumber is the facing half the engine paired this one with, both null when the half has no partner yet. Every other type reports null for both."""
type WorldLogisticsEntity { name: String! type: String! position: Position! direction: Int! unitNumber: UnitNumber status: String lanes: [WorldLane!]! heldStack: InventoryStack pickupPosition: Position dropPosition: Position undergroundType: UndergroundBeltType pairedUnitNumber: UnitNumber fluids: [WorldFluid!]! worldInventories: [WorldInventory!]! }
"""Inserters whose actual pickup or drop target is the inspected entity, read in a separate game snapshot. Targets fall back to the entity under the arm's geometric pickup/drop position when the engine target is null, so wiring stays visible for inserters that have not run since placement or power loss."""
type InspectionLogistics { tick: Float! inserters: [ConnectedInserter!]! }
"""inserter plus the entities it takes from and drops into. pickup/drop are null only when the arm position touches nothing insertable; a wired inserter reports them even while unpowered or idle."""
type ConnectedInserter { inserter: LogisticsEndpoint! pickup: LogisticsEndpoint drop: LogisticsEndpoint }
"""One inserter, machine, container or belt endpoint. direction is the engine direction code for entities that expose one; lanes carry transport-line names and sides for belt-like entities."""
type LogisticsEndpoint { name: String! type: String! position: Position! unitNumber: UnitNumber status: String direction: Int pickupPosition: Position dropPosition: Position heldStack: InventoryStack lanes: [WorldLane!]! }
"""Total counts matching logistics entities before pagination."""
type WorldLogisticsPage { tick: Float! surface: String! force: String! area: WorldArea! pageInfo: PageInfo! logisticsEntities: [WorldLogisticsEntity!]! }
"""One belt-family entity of the tile census. lanes carry every engine transport line of the entity with its contents and mixed flag; direction is the engine direction code, so lane sides stay relative to the entity."""
type BeltTile { name: String! type: String! position: Position! direction: Int! unitNumber: UnitNumber lanes: [WorldLane!]! }
"""One belt-family census page. total and pageInfo.total are the same true matching count before pagination; tiles is the sorted slice selected by limit and offset."""
type BeltTilesPage { tick: Float! surface: String! area: WorldArea! pageInfo: PageInfo! total: Int! tiles: [BeltTile!]! }
"""A mining drill near a resource entry, or one whose mining area covers part of a patch. status is the engine entity status name (null for a drill that exposes none); coveredTiles and coveredAmount count the patch resource tiles and amount inside this drill's mining area, and are 0 for entry-level distance matches."""
type WorldDrill { name: String! position: Position! unitNumber: UnitNumber status: String coveredTiles: Int! coveredAmount: Float! }
"""Resource entities, trees, cliffs, simple entities and water-collision tiles. Nearby drills are distance matches, not proof of mining coverage."""
type WorldResourceEntry { kind: String! name: String! position: Position! amount: Float requiredFluid: String fluidAmount: Float nearbyDrills: [WorldDrill!]! }
"""Totals count matching entries before pagination; resource, obstacle and water totals partition them. Patches are connected resource-entity clusters at least one tile apart from each other, sorted by total amount descending (infinite resources sort by yield percent instead, so empty finite amounts never outrank real ore)."""
type WorldResourcesPage { tick: Float! surface: String! force: String! area: WorldArea! drillRadius: Float! pageInfo: PageInfo! resourceTotal: Int! obstacleTotal: Int! waterTotal: Int! worldEntries: [WorldResourceEntry!]! patches: [ResourcePatch!]! }
"""One connected resource patch. Bounds and centroid are computed from resource entity positions. nearbyDrills only lists drills whose mining area covers at least one tile of this patch; coveredTiles and coveredAmount are the patch tiles and amount under at least one of those drills, so they measure real mining coverage rather than proximity. Infinite resources report yieldPercent (summed tile yield percentage) with totalAmount 0. clippedByArea is true when the patch touches the scan boundary, so its tiles and amounts are partial."""
type ResourcePatch { name: String! tiles: Int! totalAmount: Float! infinite: Boolean! yieldPercent: Float! bounds: WorldArea! centroid: Position! nearbyDrills: [WorldDrill!]! coveredTiles: Int! coveredAmount: Float! clippedByArea: Boolean! }
"""Engine build check with manual-placement rules; does not check player reach, inventory or research. When the placement is refused, blockers lists colliding prototype names found anywhere in the footprint, terrain is true when any footprint tile uses one of the prototype's collision layers, and tile is the ground tile name under the position."""
type WorldPlacementResult { tick: Float! surface: String! force: String! prototype: String! position: Position! direction: Int! canPlace: Boolean! blockers: [String!]! terrain: Boolean! tile: String! }
"""Totals of one placement probe over a tile grid. Result lists are mode-coupled: blockedTiles is filled in BLOCKED_TILES mode (the default) and is empty otherwise; rows is filled only in GRID mode (one string per tile row, top row first, one character per tile, 1 placeable and 0 blocked); sites is filled only in SITES mode (rectangles largest first, origin at the top-left tile corner, never overlapping). sampled/placeable/blocked are always filled."""
type PlacementProbeResult { tick: Float! surface: String! force: String! prototype: String! direction: Int! area: WorldArea! sampled: Int! placeable: Int! blocked: Int! blockedTiles: [PlacementBlockedTile!]! rows: [String!]! sites: [PlacementSite!]! }
"""One empty tile rectangle: width and height in whole tiles starting at the origin tile corner."""
type PlacementSite { origin: Position! width: Float! height: Float! }
"""One refused tile. Blockers are colliding entity prototype names, terrain is true when the tile itself blocks this prototype, and tile is the ground tile prototype name."""
type PlacementBlockedTile { position: Position! blockers: [String!]! terrain: Boolean! tile: String! }
